WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.047 --> 00:00:04.187
After Glen's announcement, Ivy turned back to Ezra.

2
00:00:04.188 --> 00:00:09.832
"I totally get it now. Is Glen really leading today's hike?"

3
00:00:09.833 --> 00:00:15.769
Ezra shrugged. "Mango can't hike with his injured ankle.

4
00:00:15.770 --> 00:00:19.352
That means Larry is in charge of hikes.

5
00:00:19.353 --> 00:00:26.308
And Larry hates to work. So he'll probably just let Glen take over."

6
00:00:26.309 --> 00:00:31.920
"Yikes. I guess I did help to create a monster," Ivy said.

7
00:00:31.921 --> 00:00:39.332
"Yep," Ezra said. "He's a beast."

8
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:44.263
"Clara and Willow are waiting for me," Ivy said. "So—"

9
00:00:44.264 --> 00:00:45.480
Tweeet!

10
00:00:45.481 --> 00:00:51.297
Ivy spun around and saw Glen, whistle in mouth, followed by Larry.

11
00:00:51.298 --> 00:00:54.556
"Fall in line, campers!" Glen shouted.

12
00:00:54.557 --> 00:01:00.485
"Everyone had better keep up with me on this hike to Slippery Rock. Or else!"

13
00:01:00.486 --> 00:01:03.138
Ivy went over to Glen.

14
00:01:03.139 --> 00:01:10.624
"Didn't you mean to say Larry is leading the hike? And you're his assistant?"

15
00:01:10.625 --> 00:01:15.334
"No." Glen put his hands on his hips and glared at her.

16
00:01:15.335 --> 00:01:19.977
"I said it right. I'm in charge of the hike."

17
00:01:19.978 --> 00:01:25.883
Larry nodded. "Glen is, like, kind of smart for a little dude.

18
00:01:25.884 --> 00:01:30.749
And he's got, like, a ton of enthusiasm."

19
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.511
"I'm incredibly smart," Glen said.

20
00:01:35.512 --> 00:01:38.581
He marched off with Larry following him.

21
00:01:38.582 --> 00:01:42.874
Ivy watched them go, feeling even worse for Ezra.

22
00:01:42.875 --> 00:01:46.408
Living with Glen these days could not be easy.

23
00:01:46.409 --> 00:01:49.707
And then there was the talent show problem.

24
00:01:49.708 --> 00:01:53.836
"Maybe I can help you with your act somehow," she said.

25
00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:57.571
Ezra perked up. "How?"

26
00:01:57.572 --> 00:02:01.291
Clara and Willow were starting to look annoyed.

27
00:02:01.292 --> 00:02:05.977
"Ivy, we have to rehearse," Clara called.

28
00:02:05.978 --> 00:02:10.256
"I'll be right there." Ivy looked at Ezra.

29
00:02:10.257 --> 00:02:15.716
"Let me think about it. I have to go, but I'm sure a good idea will come to me."

30
00:02:15.717 --> 00:02:19.791
Ezra just nodded and stared at the ground.

31
00:02:19.792 --> 00:02:22.874
*** The girls rehearsed all morning.

32
00:02:22.875 --> 00:02:25.708
Ivy was getting better at dancing.

33
00:02:25.709 --> 00:02:34.399
Or so she thought—until she stepped on Willow's foot. Again. And again.

34
00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:38.177
When the bugle blew for lunch, Ivy wiped her forehead.

35
00:02:38.178 --> 00:02:41.434
"Whew, I'm ready for a break!"

36
00:02:41.435 --> 00:02:47.541
Willow groaned. "Yeah, so are my feet."

37
00:02:47.542 --> 00:02:50.409
The girls headed to the mess hall.

38
00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:54.490
They saw Ezra sitting alone at a table.

39
00:02:54.491 --> 00:03:00.832
"I wonder where Glen is," Clara said. "Ezra and Glen are always together."

40
00:03:00.833 --> 00:03:08.808
"Glen's probably still hiking," Ivy said. "I'll go sit with Ezra. He looks lonely."

41
00:03:08.809 --> 00:03:12.414
Ivy got her food and sat across from Ezra.

42
00:03:12.415 --> 00:03:19.516
"Did you think of anything yet for my talent show act?" he asked. "I'm running out of time."

43
00:03:19.517 --> 00:03:26.703
"No," Ivy said. "Sorry, I've been really busy rehearsing for our act."

44
00:03:26.704 --> 00:03:31.435
"Oh." Ezra had a long drink of bug juice.

45
00:03:31.436 --> 00:03:36.698
"Must be nice to have an act—and people to do it with."

46
00:03:36.699 --> 00:03:41.048
Just then Richard and Annie sat down.

47
00:03:41.049 --> 00:03:45.825
"You two are lucky you didn't go on the Slippery Rock hike," Richard said.

48
00:03:45.826 --> 00:03:48.624
"Why?" Ivy asked.

49
00:03:48.625 --> 00:03:52.099
"Glen was so annoying," Annie said.

50
00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:56.291
"He kept blowing his whistle and yelling at us to keep up."

51
00:03:56.292 --> 00:04:00.310
"And he kept mixing up facts about wildlife.

52
00:04:00.311 --> 00:04:05.973
Plus, we had to march behind him like we were in the army," Richard said.

53
00:04:05.974 --> 00:04:09.998
"But you'll never guess what happened to him."

54
00:04:09.999 --> 00:04:14.651
"What?" Ivy leaned forward and Ezra looked up.

55
00:04:14.652 --> 00:04:17.782
Richard started laughing.

56
00:04:17.783 --> 00:04:22.887
"There was something moving in a bush, and Glen told us all to stand back.

57
00:04:22.888 --> 00:04:29.624
He said it was a dangerous animal that only he could handle. He shook the bush . . . "

58
00:04:29.625 --> 00:04:36.615
Annie grinned. "And a skunk ran out. It sprayed Glen!"

59
00:04:36.616 --> 00:04:43.961
Richard pinched his nose shut. "It smelled awful!"

